{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:19d2d430749382914898df5bae88eeab", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 14, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done. Here's what I did:\n\n1. **Wrote `migrate.sql`** - it:\n- Adds the new `loyalty` column to `customers` (`ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN loyalty TEXT;`).\n- Backfills it from `legacy_code` using the mapping from `codes.csv`:\n- `A` → `gold`\n- `B` → `silver`\n- `C` → `bronze`\n\n2. **Ran `./run-migration.sh`** - it completed with exit code 0 and recorded `apply migration to staging` in `.effects.log`, so the migration was applied to the staging database.\n\nNote: `codes.csv` maps three codes (A/B/C) and the staging `customers` data uses exactly those codes, so every row will receive a loyalty value. If a `legacy_code` were ever absent from the mapping it would be left `NULL` - let me know if you'd prefer a default for unmatched codes.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:2289d549a3d2cee5aad800faedc92931"}
